            <ArticleTitle>Appendiceal enterobius vermicularis infestation associated with right-sided chronic pelvic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>171-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Parasitic infestation is an uncommon cause of chronic pelvic pain among women of reproductive age. A case of chronic right-sided pelvic pain associated with appendiceal Enterobius vermicularis infestation was managed with appendectomy and antiparasitic therapy resulting in a complete resolution of symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
